know that the Integrated Assessment Tool algorithm is flawed. We know that the Integrated Assessment Tool is consistently underassessing older people's care needs, and we know, from the answers that the minister continues to give, that the government is not fully alive to this issue. It is urgent that we suspend standing orders to debate this motion because we know that tiny differences in this flawed algorithm are seeing some people having their care support halved. We know that it is urgent, and we should suspend standing orders to debate this because people like Sean Dorney—who's had motor neurone disease for a decade, who has sought a reassessment and who is not eligible for th","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-senate-10682","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2026-08-18/7"}
